## 4. What this resolves for the observation bridge

Even a perfect fit to every original click history would not determine the
number-sector energy offsets in this family. Fitting count rates or a
background-corrected coincidence cannot alone establish energy absorbed per
photon, the energy supplied at formation, or reservoir conservation. An
additional physically identified energy measurement or a phase-sensitive
number-changing reference could distinguish the family. Neither is supplied
as a new apparatus here. The native selection of h, its inter-sector energy
convention and a physical source/reservoir must be justified independently.

This does not invalidate the fixed-h mathematics or rule out observational
agreement. Counts can constrain the parts of the model to which they are
sensitive. Equation(6) shows a surviving energy distinction, and measurements
outside the count algebra remain open. The finite counting capacity from the
main formation-balance source remains separately relevant to a stationary
source: altering f(N) does not replenish its record slots.

